# project: nightly-release-train
// Fully autonomous nightly release train: build, test, deploy, monitor,
// auto-rollback and requeue. Runs every night, weekends included.

VAR deploy_attempts = 0

-> await_window

=== await_window ===
Nightly departure window: the train leaves every night, weekends included, carrying whatever changes are queued.
Done when tonight's window opens and the ship-or-idle call is made autonomously.
~ deploy_attempts = 0
+ [Changes queued, train departs] -> build
+ [Nothing to ship tonight, idle until tomorrow] ~loop~ -> await_window
+ [Retire the release train] @human -> END

=== build ===
Build tonight's release artifact from the queued changes.
Done when a versioned, reproducible artifact exists.
+ [Build succeeded] -> test
+ [Build failed, changes ride tomorrow's train] ~loop~ -> await_window

=== test ===
Run the full automated test suite against tonight's artifact.
Done when every suite is green; no human review of results.
+ [All tests green] -> deploy
+ [Tests failed, release requeued for tomorrow night] ~loop~ -> await_window

=== deploy ===
Deploy tonight's artifact to production, fully unattended.
Done when the new release is serving live traffic.
~ deploy_attempts += 1
+ [Deploy is live] -> monitor
+ {deploy_attempts < 5} [Deploy failed, retry now] ~loop~ -> deploy
+ {deploy_attempts >= 5} [Tonight's retry budget spent, release rides tomorrow's train] ~loop~ -> await_window

=== monitor ===
Watch production health signals for the new release; monitoring is continuous and the train never stops on its own.
Done for this cycle when the release is judged healthy or an incident is traced to it.
+ [Incident traced to this release] -> rollback
+ [Release healthy, keep monitoring until the next window] ~loop~ -> await_window

=== rollback ===
Automatically roll back to the previous known-good release, no human sign-off.
Done when the rollback is live and the failed release is requeued for the next night's train.
+ [Rolled back, release back on the train] ~loop~ -> await_window
